# Telltale environment variables
#
# The core experience requires NO configuration and no API keys. Clone, install
# and run: the app falls back to an embedded PGlite database and every live source
# is keyless.
#
# Only production needs a variable, and only one.

# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION.
# Neon Postgres (or any Postgres) connection string. Without it a production build
# refuses to start rather than silently using the embedded local store.
DATABASE_URL=

# OPTIONAL. Overrides the site metadata base URL, sitemap, OpenGraph URLs and the
# repository-facing links in the footer. Must be the public production alias, with
# no trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# OPTIONAL. Absolute path to the embedded PGlite data directory used for local
# development and tests. Defaults to ./.pglite
TELLTALE_PGLITE_DIR=./.pglite

# LOCAL VERIFICATION ONLY. Set to 1 to let `next build && next start` run without
# DATABASE_URL. Never set this on a real deployment: it re-enables the embedded
# store.
TELLTALE_ALLOW_EMBEDDED_STORE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark runner, optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `npm run bench:kaggle` needs your own Kaggle credentials to create a benchmark and
# run it against the Kaggle model catalogue. Nothing in the app needs them. Point
# the runner at an existing kaggle.json, or set these two variables. Never commit
# a key: kaggle.json is gitignored and these are read at run time only.
#
# KAGGLE_USERNAME=
# KAGGLE_KEY=